 "scope": "Producer development observations only, unsigned; no timing, independent execution proof, new global selector, target-solving advantage, or novelty claim. Both earlier 60-second timeouts are preserved; full coverage uses separately sealed fixture/public-point calls.",
 "statement": "The frozen native local-torsion evaluator, which takes no input scalar, passes the planned seven precisions through p^64 on all 18 and 82 nonidentity points of the p17/order19 and p257/order83 fixtures and on four hash-derived public secp256k1 points. Separate Jacobian arithmetic checks torsion, the small-fixture scalar relations, and secp256k1 negation/addition; OpenSSL checks source arithmetic. This is a classical source-local lifting component, not a cross-prime transfer."
